<template>
    <heading>Controller</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>controller</li>
        <li>command dispatch</li>
        <li>handler stack</li>
        <li>initialization</li>
        <li>state machine</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p>Command dispatch is a kind of hierarchical state machine, implemented with a stack where push is a "call" and pop is a "return".</p>
        <p>Each command is an object with at least a <code>name</code> field identifying the command. Additional fields carry its arguments. The controller passes the same object to each handler involved in dispatch.</p>
        <p><code>dispatch(command)</code> queues command handling in a microtask, allowing the current handler to suspend before another command reaches it. Producers of async completion commands use this default method without scheduling their own microtasks. <code>dispatchImmediate(command)</code> handles a command synchronously; use it when an operation must call a browser API during the originating user activation, such as the Select button opening the directory picker. Parent/child handoffs remain synchronous within either form of dispatch.</p>
        <p>Both dispatch methods throw an explicit error until initialization installs the command handler. Each handler is a generator object. Call <code>init(handler)</code> once to install the first handler. The stack is undefined until initialization creates it. An empty stack still records that initialization has occurred, so a second call throws an error even after dispatch removes the last handler.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>JavaScript units</name>
        <code><![CDATA[let controller = (() => {
    let handlerStack; // top of stack is current command handler

    function init(handler) {
        if (handlerStack !== undefined)
            throw new Error("Controller has already been initialized");
        handlerStack = [handler];
        result.dispatch = dispatch;
        result.dispatchImmediate = baseCommandHandler;
    }

    function dispatch(command) {
        queueMicrotask(() => baseCommandHandler(command));
    }

    function notInitialized() {
        throw new Error("Controller has not been initialized");
    }

    function baseCommandHandler(command) {
        for (let handler; (handler = handlerStack.at(-1)) !== undefined; ) {
            let result = handler.next(command);
            if (result.done)
                handlerStack.pop()
            else if (result.value === handler) // keep same handler
                return;
            else
                handlerStack.push(result.value);
        }
    }

    let result = {
        init: init,
        dispatch: notInitialized,
        dispatchImmediate: notInitialized
    };
    return result;
})();
]]></code>
    </section>
</template>
